𒑰 DUB.SAR 1.0 Example: Persistent Tablet Sequences
𒑰 Difficulty: Mastery
𒑰 Concept: Persistent Sequence Inscription
𒑰 Mode: Mixed (Cuneiform syntax with Latin identifiers)
𒑰
𒑰 Purpose:
𒑰   Inscribes a working sequence tablet into the persistent SQLite archive
𒑰   under name 'powers', consults it, and inspects length and terminal entries.
𒑰
𒑰 Expected Output:
𒑰   5
𒑰   1
𒑰   16

𒂊𒁹

    working powers of length 0
    powers 1 𒈭
    powers 2 𒈭
    powers 4 𒈭
    powers 8 𒈭
    powers 16 𒈭

    inscribe tablet powers

    𒅆 𒁾 "powers"
    n : powers 𒁍
    first_power : powers first
    last_power : powers last

𒅗𒁹

    n
    first_power
    last_power
